<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB wins $150 mln Saudi order.</title>
<headline>ABB wins $150 mln Saudi order.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG said it had signed an order from the Saudi Consolidated Electric Co. in the Eastern Province of Saudi Arabia (SCEO) for a major high-voltage substation near Jubail on the Arabian Gulf.  </p>
<p>The turnkey order is valued at $150 million and work will start immediately. Completion is scheduled for April 1999, ABB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The substation will integrate a new 2,400-megawatt power plant into the SCECO East power grid and improve the reliability of electricity supplies to industries in the Jubail area.</p>
<p>ABB will supply, install and commission 380- and 230- kilovolt gas-insulated switchgear comprising 33 circuit breakers, together with four 750-mega volt ampere power transformers.</p>
<p>ABB will also supply the associated control, protection and communications equipment, it said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
